  description: Uranus is the seventh planet from the Sun and an ice giant composed
    mainly of hydrogen, helium, and materials such as water, ammonia, and methane.
    Methane in its atmosphere absorbs red light, giving the planet its distinctive
    blue-green color.
  interestingFact: Uranus rotates almost entirely on its side, with an axial tilt
    of approximately 98 degrees.
